535322 true] [17592186343672 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535322 true] [17592186343672 1100 "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139535322 true] [17592186343672 1113 #uuid "f8f4a5ce-40a5-520d-b284-4547a3fc3317" 13194139535322 true] [17592186343672 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343674 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343675 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343676 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343677 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343678 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1041 "selection" 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343674 13194139535322 true] [17592186343673 1110 #uuid "93534edc-2253-5472-b70f-366595869299" 13194139535322 true] [17